{%- comment -%}
  Lena: product breadcrumbs — Home > [Category] > [Piece name]

  Category resolution, in order:
    1. `collection` — populated only when the visitor arrived via
       /collections/<handle>/products/<handle>. This also covers parent collections
       that are deliberately not in the menu (e.g. signature-purses), so arriving
       through one still renders a correct trail.
    2. The product's first collection matching the menu category list below.
    3. Neither — fall back to a two-crumb trail.

  Accepts: product (required), collection (optional)

  `collection` is passed in explicitly rather than relied on as a global: {% render %}
  isolates scope, and a silently-nil object here would downgrade every breadcrumb to
  the two-crumb fallback without erroring.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  capture lena_cat_csv
    render 'lena-category-handles'
  endcapture
  assign lena_menu_categories = lena_cat_csv | strip | split: ','

  assign lena_crumb_title = blank
  assign lena_crumb_url = blank

  if collection != blank and collection.handle != blank and collection.handle != 'all'
    assign lena_crumb_title = collection.title
    assign lena_crumb_url = collection.url
  else
    for lena_c in product.collections
      if lena_menu_categories contains lena_c.handle
        assign lena_crumb_title = lena_c.title
        assign lena_crumb_url = lena_c.url
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

<nav class="lena-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    {%- comment -%}
      The current page is deliberately NOT a crumb. It would repeat the <h1>
      immediately beneath it word for word, and on these product titles that
      wraps the trail onto a second line for no added information. The point of
      this nav is the way back to the category, not a restatement of where you
      already are.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if lena_crumb_title != blank -%}
      <li><a href="{{ lena_crumb_url }}">{{ lena_crumb_title | escape }}</a></li>
    {%- endif -%}
  </ol>
</nav>
